{"slug":"move-zeros-to-end","title":"Move Zeros to the End","topic":"arrays-strings","difficulty":"easy","order":104,"tags":["arrays","two-pointers"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"A write index","body":["To keep some elements and drop others, walk over the array with a **read index** `i` and keep a second index `w`, the **write index**, that marks where the next kept element goes. When `a[i]` is kept, copy it to `a[w]` and add one to `w`.",{"code":"w = 0\nfor i in range(n):\n    if a[i] != 0:\n        a[w] = a[i]\n        w += 1"},"The write index never passes the read index, so nothing is overwritten before it has been read. After the loop, the first `w` places hold the kept elements in their original order."]},"statement":["Move all zeros of an array to the end. The other numbers must keep their relative order."],"inputFormat":["The first line has `n`.","The second line has `n` integers."],"outputFormat":["Print the changed array on one line."],"constraints":["1 <= n <= 1000","-10^9 <= each number <= 10^9"],"examples":[{"input":"6\n0 1 0 3 12 0\n","output":"1 3 12 0 0 0\n","note":"The non-zero numbers 1 3 12 come first, then three zeros."}],"hints":["Copy the non-zero numbers to the front, in order.","Use a write index `w` that grows only when you keep a number.","After the copy, fill the places from `w` to the end with zeros."],"starter":{"python":"n = int(input())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> a[i];\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n        long[] a = new long[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) a[i] = sc.nextLong();\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["Copy every non-zero element to the write index, then fill the rest with zeros. The relative order of the non-zero numbers is kept because we read from left to right."],"complexity":"Time O(n), space O(1).","code":{"python":"n = int(input())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\nw = 0\nfor i in range(n):\n    if a[i] != 0:\n        a[w] = a[i]\n        w += 1\nwhile w < n:\n    a[w] = 0\n    w += 1\nprint(*a)\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> a[i];\n\n    int w = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        if (a[i] != 0) a[w++] = a[i];\n    }\n    while (w < n) a[w++] = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cout << a[i] << (i + 1 < n ? \" \" : \"\\n\");\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n        long[] a = new long[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) a[i] = sc.nextLong();\n\n        int w = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            if (a[i] != 0) a[w++] = a[i];\n        }\n        while (w < n) a[w++] = 0;\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) sb.append(a[i]).append(i + 1 < n ? \" \" : \"\\n\");\n        System.out.print(sb);\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"6\n0 1 0 3 12 0\n","output":"1 3 12 0 0 0\n"},{"input":"1\n0\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"1\n4\n","output":"4\n"},{"input":"3\n0 0 0\n","output":"0 0 0\n"},{"input":"4\n1 2 3 4\n","output":"1 2 3 4\n"},{"input":"4\n0 0 5 6\n","output":"5 6 0 0\n"},{"input":"25\n2 2 1 -1 0 -2 2 0 -2 -2 2 1 1 0 0 2 0 2 -1 0 1 -2 1 -2 1\n","output":"2 2 1 -1 -2 2 -2 -2 2 1 1 2 2 -1 1 -2 1 -2 1 0 0 0 0 0 0\n"},{"input":"1000\n1 1 -1 0 1 0 -1 1 0 1 1 